    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13975" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποτάδην</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰδ</span>], Adv., (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τείνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stretched at length,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Zeux.</u>
				4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				4.21
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τρέχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					6.175
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>diffusely, prolixly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VS</u>
				1
			</span></i>
            <u>Praef.</u>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1.15.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξυνέστειλε τοὺς χοροὺς ἀ. ὄντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>VA</u>
					6.11
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. φθεγγόμενον [φθέγμα
			κηρύκων</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.94
			</span></i>; also with 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατά, τῶν κατὰ ἀ. λόγων ἀκήκοας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herm.
					<u>in Phdr.</u>
					p.184A.
				</span></i>
			</div>
